            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "## What a README Is For\n\nA README is the first document someone reads about a project. It explains what the project does and how to get started with it, without requiring the reader to dig through the source code.\n\n- **Orientation:** describes the project's purpose and key features\n- **Setup:** lists requirements and installation steps\n- **Usage:** shows how to run or use the project, with examples\n\nExample of a typical install-and-run section:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/example/project.git\ncd project\nnpm install && npm start\n```\n\n| Section | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| Description | What the project is |\n| Installation | How to set it up |"
            }
          ],
